  "truthBoundary": "A42 detects mixed-pass source trees, validates bounded source JSON, sanitizes inherited private Next.js variables, invalidates only generated .next state, defaults Windows development to Webpack, and provides one bounded Turbopack-to-Webpack recovery plus an HTTP smoke contract. It preserves A41 route recovery and stop-sell. It does not by itself prove exact browser rendering, provider availability, staging, LIVE operation, or sale readiness. A43 closes the observed Webpack CSS Modules pure-selector failure and adds a preflight scanner; exact user-machine rerun remains required. A102R32 adds the imported route-transition policy to the critical dev fingerprint and updates exact current hashes after invalid/missing hash timeout plus prefetch-intent reentry recovery. This remains a development bootstrap contract and grants no exact build/browser, LIVE or sale credit.",
